commit 5f5d2470bfd520601f711974918f3ddde60bedb0

C03: an identity question has its own presentation; how-it-works may not claim universal behaviours (IDENTITY1327)

IDENTITY1325 measured: «to quien chuta eres.» got a knowledge reply confused by «chuta» («No sé a quién chuta…»); «cómo funciona esto» named the served catalog but closed with «siempre preguntando antes de cambiar algo», and its English pair invented «always watching and listening».

llm: presentation shape identity for every identity question (anchors name/runs_on; contract: names BAXY, asks nothing back). HOW_IT_WORKS prompt forbids behaviour claims beyond the catalog; its contract rejects siempre/always/constantly, watching/listening/monitoring.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


